<h1>Glossary: Frameworks &amp; Certifications</h1>

<div class="col root"><div class="row"><div><div style="font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#4493f8">TERM</div></div>
<div><div style="font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#4493f8">MEANING</div></div></div>
<div class="card"><div class="t">SOC 2</div><div class="d">Audit standard for SaaS operations (security, availability, confidentiality) - proof-of-controls report by an independent CPA firm.</div></div>
<div class="card"><div class="t">HIPAA</div><div class="d">US law protecting health data (PHI); mandatory for healthcare workloads.</div></div>
<div class="card"><div class="t">PCI-DSS</div><div class="d">Payment card industry security standard; mandatory for anything touching card data (including your token-budget/billing flows).</div></div>
<div class="card"><div class="t">NIST CSF</div><div class="d">US framework catalog for security programs; the &quot;N&quot; in many evidence-pack exports.</div></div>
<div class="card"><div class="t">CIS Benchmarks</div><div class="d">Center for Internet Security best-practice configuration catalogs (e.g., AWS Foundations Benchmark) that posture tools score against.</div></div>
<div class="card"><div class="t">GDPR / DSGVO</div><div class="d">EU data protection law - the reason security tooling must prove what it stores, not just that it stores it.</div></div></div>


</body>
